I reviewed all three commits on this branch (the removal of the RFC 8693 jurisdiction-token exchange in favor of using the login JWT directly for cell/git-transport auth), across `cell_data_api.go`, `refresh.go`, `env_token.go`, and `cmd/git-remote-entire/main.go` plus their tests.

The refactor is internally consistent: the `--jurisdiction` exchange path (`JurisdictionToken`) and its SSRF guards (`requireSafeExchangeURL`) are preserved untouched, the new `refreshingProvider`/`RefreshingLoginCredential` reactive-refresh-on-401 mechanism in `git-remote-entire` correctly single-flights within the (single-threaded, per-process) proxy, dangling references to the removed `jurisdictionauth.go` types (`jurisdictionTokenSource`, `mintSlot`, `RememberJurisdictionAudience` caller) are all cleaned up or intentionally left for back-compat logout cleanup, and the test suite was updated in lockstep with the behavioral change. I did not find a distinct, concrete implementation bug (as opposed to the deliberate architectural change itself, which spans coordinated commits and is out of scope to second-guess without server-side context).

